  {
    "id": "8c17a304e6f4166e0302",
    "source": "Summon or bond a creature a feature grants: kind familiar (Find Familiar), beast_companion (Beast Master), drake (Drakewarden, its essence) or other (a story pet: a stat block's name, or hp and ac). A story pet with no stat block cannot attack. A Find Familiar form is bat, cat, crab, frog, hawk, lizard, octopus, owl, poisonous snake, quipper, rat, raven, sea horse, spider or weasel, or imp, quasit, pseudodragon or sprite with Pact of the Chain. A Beast Master companion is a Medium or smaller beast of CR 1/4 or lower. A story pet named for an SRD creature (mastiff, wolf, riding horse) or a monster the table made in the workshop takes that stat block, and fights with it when its CR is no higher than a druid of the owner's level could become (1/4, 1/2 from 4th level, 1 from 8th). The server validates the feature, loads the stat block, and attaches the pet to their sheet. Call it BEFORE narrating the summon.",
    "sourceHash": "8c17a304e6f4166e03028cb10640ad640678e79aa3f1e374860c3ca8520b0190",
